    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d915">

                <pb facs="1134" n="1124" xml:id="pg1124"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">102.1/5–2247: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Stuart</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-05-22T18:00:00-04:00">May 22, 1947—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>608. To Adler from Treasury. Authorize compromise omission of reference to “both
                    parties” or “either party,” preferring, however, inclusion following in exchange
                    of letters: “arrangement is subject to review by both parties from time to time
                    in light of changing circumstances.” If necessary to reach agreement authorize
                    acceptance Chinese position on this point. [Treasury.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
